  "historical_output_text": " I appreciate the insight! Comparative purchases like this one between coffee at $4 vs tea can vary widely based upon personal taste or brand choices, so let that inform the decision! \n\nWhile it can cost about 4-7% as expensive, the tea leaves are also less refined compared so they may contain beneficial nutrients that the processed beans lack. However coffee is much higher stimulatory and contains caffeine for a bigger buzz and longer effects.\n\nOn taste, many prefer the more complex, full-bodied, nuanced taste that can vary greatly with coffee. With so few steps from bean -> brewed, a lot is packed into one cup of the strong stuff.\n\nTeaware and tea rituals may be less accessible but can provide their charms as meditative practice. And a lot more flavor options to try!\n\nWhat factors are guiding the choices of you? Do any others compare",
